        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HINDI vs URDU:\n  Spoken Hindustani (everyday speech) is essentially the same language.\n  A native Hindi and Urdu speaker can fully understand each other in conversation.\n  DIVERGENCE at formal registers:\n    Hindi formal → Sanskrit-derived vocabulary\n    Urdu formal → Persian/Arabic-derived vocabulary\n  SCRIPT:\n    Hindi → Devanagari (left-to-right)\n    Urdu → Nastaliq calligraphic script (right-to-left, Arabic-derived)\n  Political: Hindi is national language of India; Urdu is of Pakistan.\n```"
    },
