      "text": "```\nDEVANAGARI — The script of Hindi (and Sanskrit, Marathi, Nepali)\n=================================================================\nType: Abugida — each symbol is a consonant with inherent 'a' vowel.\n      Vowels other than inherent 'a' are written as diacritical marks.\nDirection: Left to right, top bar (शिरोरेखा shirorēkhā) connects letters."
    },
    {
      "id": "08-HINDI-URDU.md#007",
      "path": [
        "08-HINDI-URDU.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
