      "text": "CONJUNCT CONSONANTS — when two consonants touch (no vowel between):\n  क + ष = क्ष  [kṣa] — common in Sanskrit loanwords\n  त + र = त्र  [tra]\n  ज + ञ = ज्ञ  [jña/gna]\n  These are new characters, not obvious from parts."
    },
