      "text": "RETROFLEX CONSONANTS — tongue curled back to palate:\n  ट ड ण ठ ढ — vs dental counterparts त द न\n  Hindi \"ṭ\" (retroflex) vs \"t\" (dental) — phonemically distinct.\n  English has only one \"t\". Hindi has two.\n  \"पत\" vs \"पट\" — different words."
